1
00:00:01,240 --> 00:00:11,490
Right this way, Mr. and Mrs. Stewart.

2
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:14,360
Well, it's small, but clean.

3
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:22,230
Clean? You call this clean?

4
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,160
Have a nice stay.

5
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:33,490
Thank you. I don't believe this.

6
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:39,990
Well, it isn't the Watermill Inn,

7
00:00:39,990 --> 00:00:52,640
but let's get a look at the view.

8
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,670
How is the view?

9
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:59,570
Great, if you enjoy looking at a parking lot.

10
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:03,630
Well, maybe we'll see the view in the morning.

11
00:01:03,630 --> 00:01:21,780
Right now, we should clean up this room.

12
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:24,170
Sorry, Marilyn.

13
00:01:24,170 --> 00:01:26,560
Why should you be sorry?

14
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:31,840
Well, the rain, the room, the view of the parking lot.

15
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,890
It isn't the way I hoped it would be.

16
00:01:34,890 --> 00:01:37,930
Stop blaming yourself.

17
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:45,400
After all, we're here, we're alone, we're together.

18
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:49,870
And I love you. Isn't that enough?

19
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:50,730
It is for me,

20
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:55,430
but I wanted this weekend to be special for you.

21
00:01:55,430 --> 00:02:05,540
It is special. Happy anniversary.

22
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,990
It's still raining. I want to play tennis.

23
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:10,880
I want some breakfast.

24
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,600
Let's call room service and order a nice breakfast,

25
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:16,090
and then we'll figure out what to do today.

26
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:24,920
Right. Would you give me room service, please?

27
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:34,380
I beg your pardon? Oh, I see.

28
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:38,770
They don't have room service at Old Country Inn.

29
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:42,600
Well, let's go down to the coffee shop.

30
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,040
They don't have a coffee shop.

31
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:51,800
We can get our meals at Mrs. Montefiore's down the road.

32
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,340
That's OK, honey.

33
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,110
I love walking in the rain.

34
00:02:55,110 --> 00:02:58,920
Oh, you're being a really good sport about this, Marilyn,

35
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,540
but I think we should face the truth.

36
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,190
What's that?

37
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:05,540
This is not the way to spend our fifth anniversary.

38
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:09,420
Well, what do you want to do?

39
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:11,750
Why don't we get in the car and drive home?

40
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:15,260
Oh, Richard, it really isn't that bad.

41
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:20,250
Do you want to stick it out for the whole weekend?

42
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:22,730
Well, I'll admit the room is uncomfortable.

43
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:24,930
Uh-hum.

44
00:03:24,930 --> 00:03:26,630
And I do feel bad about your mother

45
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:30,240
having to take care of the baby all weekend.

46
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:31,680
Why don't we just check out?

47
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:39,740
OK.

48
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:44,480
Hello? Yes. Yes, this is she.

49
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:49,360
Oh, hello! How nice of you to remember us!

50
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:52,480
Yes, my husband did call.

51
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:58,910
You do? Really? It won't be any trouble?

52
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:04,360
Oh, yes, I think we'd like that very much.

53
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:13,410
Fifteen minutes! Thank you. Good-bye.

54
00:04:13,410 --> 00:04:15,810
You will never guess.

55
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:18,620
Uh ... I give up.

56
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:24,080
Mrs. Montefiore from the Watermill Inn.

57
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:26,700
What is she calling about?

58
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:28,360
They have an opening.

59
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,660
Someone just checked out.

60
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:34,110
and Mrs. Montefiore has reserved the honeymoon suite for us.

61
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:34,780
You're kidding!

62
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:37,230
No. Isn't it wonderful?

63
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:38,730
It's fantastic!

64
00:04:38,730 --> 00:04:43,380
Oh. Now all it has to do is stop raining.

65
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:46,380
Let's go.
